x86_64-linux  the difference is COMDAT, not the operator. cxx1 emits a function defined inside its class as an ordinary definition; clang emits it linkonce_odr in a COMDAT section, which the name collector does not see - so cxx1 lists constructors, destructors and inline members that clang has too and has hidden. Same root as tests/cases/dynamic-cast.nonames, and the same thing that makes vtables and type_infos collide across translation units: this compiler has no weak or linkonce linkage at all. It is not about this case, and it is older than it. What this case is for - that the operator resolves and answers the right value - is checked by run.sh on all three machines and by emit.sh for all three targets.
